## 14. Measurement framework

### Brand and trust

- Unaided and aided awareness;
- Association with performance, inclusivity, and authenticity;
- Product-claim comprehension;
- Trust in the official store;
- Brand-search growth;
- Positive and negative sentiment by topic;
- Creator credibility;
- Consumer understanding of Asian heritage versus local adaptation.

### Commercial performance

- First-purchase conversion;
- Customer acquisition cost by channel;
- Contribution margin after shipping, returns, creator fees, and marketplace commissions;
- Marketplace-to-owned migration where consent and platform rules permit;
- Average order value;
- Repeat purchase at 60, 90, and 180 days;
- Bundle attachment;
- Loyalty enrollment;
- Regional and city-level demand;
- Payment failure and fraud rates.

### Product fit

- Rating and review themes;
- Shade mismatch and exchange rates;
- Repeat purchase by product and shade;
- Stockouts by shade depth;
- Texture, fragrance, packaging, and climate complaints;
- Adverse-event reports;
- Sample-to-full-size conversion;
- Routine completion and product compatibility.

### Community commerce

- Revenue per active partner;
- Customer repeat purchase independent of partner recruitment;
- Advice satisfaction;
- Claims violations;
- unsolicited-message complaints;
- Commission concentration;
- Partner retention;
- Percentage of partners purchasing inventory—ideally none beyond personal use;
- Recruitment-related complaints—target zero.

### Channel health

- Owned versus marketplace profitability;
- Official-store share of marketplace sales;
- Unauthorized seller prevalence;
- Fulfillment time;
- Return resolution;
- WhatsApp response and conversion;
- Live-commerce view-to-purchase conversion;
- Creator incrementality rather than last-click attribution alone.

